From: Will Faust <willtechnoduck@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 18:29:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Clarify what each branch offers, and what was already granted

The notice said Madeira's commits are GPL while also saying earlier permissive
grants stand, without reconciling the two. Both are true and the resolution is
the branch split, which the notice did not explain.

ios-mythic through 61f5b29 keeps its prior permissive grants; the same material
is re-offered under the GPL on ios-madeira. The replayed commits are therefore
available either way, which is an unavoidable consequence of having published
them permissively first. Only contributions first published after the migration
are GPL-only, because only those carry no earlier grant.

Added at the tip rather than replayed through the history, since rewriting a
branch again to fix prose would be more disruptive than the fix is worth.

Madeira-commit: e60293eb1fac2e75c2e8524cc22de8ae2c0c23da
Rebased: clean
Class: madeira-port
